{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Sketchy Bee 🐝","id":"297577343554158603","is_bot":0,"username":"sketchybee"},"author_id":"297577343554158603","channel_id":"736444701149757610","content":"*Goblins and enclosed spaces do not mix well.* Despite being dexterous, Leaf has been inside only three places before now (Museum for the fight, the Mason's temple and the Fat Friar a grand total of two times). In her first days here she was extremely on edge and clumsy, not used to hard metal under her feet. Leaf also doesn't have shoes, so her toe claws click against the metal and it makes her very comfortable and self conscious. If your character is an early riser they may have caught her attempting to file them down a few times. \n\nIt's not all bad though. Each morning Leaf tends to her flower bed- as in on her first day here she dumped all the seeds from her pockets into her bed. After only a few days of Druidcraft her entire bed began to sprout grass and flowers of all kinds. Hopefully none of you have seasonal allergies...\n\nIn addition to this routine , every evening before bed, when she would usually be looking up at the stars with the Rooftopgang, she sits on her flower bed with her carved holy symbol in her lap, silently praying to the Wild Mother. Despite her unfamiliarity with it, the ocean cradling the ship brings her comfort, and she thanks Melora for each day they are allowed to pass peacefully. She attributes this to your uneventful passage so far, but who knows how long the peace will last.","created_at":"2020-07-25T09:15:27.313000Z","edited_at":"2020-07-25T09:15:49.424000Z","id":"736511927781556266","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
